{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# J2 — Extract the Jira-family shared layer out of the Cloud adapter\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`adapters/jira/` currently owns units that are Jira-family-general, not Cloud-specific: the local↔Jira field\nmaps and value maps (`outbound_fields.py`), the sanitizers (`jira_fields.py`, `comment_limits.py`), the\n`rebar-id` identity convention (`identity.py`), the link relation vocabulary\n(`jira_fields._RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`), and the absence-probe classifier (`probe.py`). PR #120 consumed these\nfrom a second adapter as **private** cross-package imports, which ADR 0035 never sanctioned — its seam is one\nlevel deep, core ⇄ adapter, with `adapters/jira/` as one backend's concrete implementation.\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/` and move those units into it with **public**\nnames, then re-point the Cloud adapter's imports. Behavior is unchanged and proven so by the characterization\noracles pinned in J1 [rebar:acb2-1823-2f0d-415b], which must pass untouched across this change.\n\nPer ADR 0035 decision 4, **no re-export shims** are left at the old paths: tests patch module-qualified, so a\nshim would create a patch-binding bug. Every importer and every `mock.patch` string is updated in this same\nchange, and each moved module keeps exactly one canonical path. The move set is chosen to avoid the\nfile-location loader entirely — none of these modules is reached by `lazy_load` / `_load_sibling_keyed` /\n`spec_from_file_location`, so the dynamic loader is untouched, matching how ADR 0035 Phase 1 sequenced its own\nrelocation.\n\n`adapters/jira/`'s ACLI transport (`acli*.py`) is explicitly **not** moved and not modified: it is the\nCloud-specific, live-validated part.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** promoting these into the backend-neutral core. They are Jira-specific — a GitHub\nbackend would want none of them — so the neutral core is the wrong home and would re-create the coupling ADR\n0035's Phase 2 removed.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** leaving them in `adapters/jira/` and importing across adapters (PR #120's approach).\nIt makes a concrete backend double as a shared library with no contract, and points a dependency edge sideways\nbetween siblings.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/` (new package).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/` — `outbound_fields.py`, `jira_fields.py`,\n  `comment_limits.py`, `identity.py`, `probe.py` relocated; `backend.py` imports updated; `acli*.py` untouched.\n- Every internal importer and every test `mock.patch` string naming the old paths.\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier plus the pinned characterization oracles: the mechanism is a relocation, so the oracle is that\nobservable behavior is identical and that no import or patch target dangles.\n\n- happy path: the full existing suite passes, including J1's exact-value characterization assertions, with no\n  edits to those assertions.\n- structural oracle: a test asserts no module under `adapters/jira_datacenter/` or `adapters/jira/` imports a\n  name prefixed `_` from the other adapter package — pinning the \"no cross-adapter private imports\" rule this\n  epic exists to establish.\n- negative control: `grep` confirms no re-export shim module remains at any old path.\n- collateral invariant: the reconciler's dynamic loader still resolves every by-path module (the existing\n  loader tests pass unchanged), proving no location-pinned file was moved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make test` passes with J1's characterization assertions unmodified\n- [ ] `grep -rn 'adapters\\.jira\\.' src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/` returns nothing\n      once J7 lands, and in this story no module under `adapters/jira/` imports from a sibling adapter\n- [ ] no re-export shim exists at any pre-move path (verified by `grep` for the old module names)\n- [ ] every `mock.patch(` string in `tests/` naming a moved module resolves to the new path (`make test` green\n      is the check, since a stale patch target raises)\n- [ ] `adapters/jira/acli*.py` are byte-identical to their pre-change state (`git diff --stat` shows no change)"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785010365524619001,"uuid":"07e23e80-f998-46a6-9b7a-b4a5e6df01f2"}